4.3    Ljung-Box Test and Box-Pierce Test
                信




    In order to perform statistical tests, we make the following assumptions：

                                      𝐻0 : 𝜌 1 = 𝜌 2 = . . . = 𝜌 ℎ = 0                                   (7)
      微




   The values of the lag-h series are mutually independent, and the sequence is composed of
independently and identically distributed white noise, namely the correlations in the population
from which the sample is taken are 0, so that any observed correlations in the data result from


                                                                                                     2
                                                                                                         关注数学模型
