6.1     Gray Relational Analysis




                                                                              数
    Grey relational analysis gauges the relationship between sequences by comparing their geometric

                                                        ：
shapes. It involves converting discrete data points into continuous line graphs using linear
interpolation. A model is then built to assess correlation based on the geometric features of these




                                                                                               els
graphs. The closer the shapes, the higher the correlation between the sequences.
                                                       号
